<title>USA: RESEARCH ALERT - Petrobras starts.</title>
<headline>RESEARCH ALERT - Petrobras starts.</headline>
<text>
<p>-- Oppenheimer &amp; Co analysts Vinod Sehgal and James Rice on Monday started coverage of Brazilian state energy company Petroleos Brasileiros, or Petrobras, with an outperform rating.</p>
<p>-- They set a price target of 225 reais, or $200.89, for Petrobras shares by the end of 1997 and predicted &quot;above-average growth with above-average risk.&quot;</p>
<p>((--Ian Simpson, Wall Street desk, (212) 859-1879))</p>
</text>
